# Runtime state Claude Code writes into ~/.claude, which is a symlink to
# .claude/ here. Declarative config stays tracked:
#
#   CLAUDE.md  README.md  settings.json  skills.manifest
#   commands/  rules/  harness/  id-workflow/  skill-library/  skills/
#
# skills/ and skill-library/ are DISJOINT halves of one set, not a copy and its
# source: skills.manifest promotes ~81 entries into skills/ (auto-invocable,
# on every session roster) and leaves the rest in skill-library/ (indexed by
# the `skill-library` skill). Neither is derivable from the other, so both are
# tracked. sync-skills.sh moves entries between them; it does not regenerate
# either from scratch.

# --- credentials and identity ---
.claude/.credentials.json

# --- session and conversation state ---
.claude/history.jsonl
.claude/projects/
.claude/sessions/
.claude/session-env/
.claude/shell-snapshots/
.claude/paste-cache/
.claude/todos/
.claude/plans/
.claude/file-history/

# --- background daemon and job runner ---
.claude/daemon/
.claude/daemon.lock
.claude/daemon.log
.claude/daemon.status.json
.claude/jobs/

# --- caches, telemetry, housekeeping ---
.claude/cache/
.claude/backups/
.claude/debug/
.claude/stats-cache.json
.claude/statsig/
.claude/.last-cleanup

# --- externally managed ---
# plugins/ holds marketplaces cloned by Claude Code (gitkraken, official LSPs).
# The one marketplace this repo owns lives in harness/, which stays tracked.
.claude/plugins/

# --- machine-local overrides ---
.claude/settings.local.json

# ~/.claude.json symlinks here (see bin/link-files-nixos). It is Claude Code's
# own mutable state -- OAuth account, onboarding flags, per-project history,
# caches -- and only its `mcpServers` key is declarative. That key's source of
# truth is the tracked .claude/mcp.json, which the linker merges in on every
# run, so nothing is lost by keeping the file itself out of git.
claude.json
